      "id": 1,
      "text": "North Norwich was carved out of the town of Norwich in 1849, giving it a distinct municipal identity.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://chenangohistorical.org/town/north-norwich/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name comes from its neighbor to the south, the city of Norwich, echoing the English city of the same name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://chenangohistorical.org/town/north-norwich/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Rea‑D‑Pack Foods, a family‑owned business, began in North Norwich in 1953 and still supplies the region today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
